CLOAK AND RING ISSUANCE
On induction each member receives standard organisation garments and one ring.

1. Cloak: black, patterned with red clouds. Collar high. Worn on all sanctioned
   operations. It marks you as Akatsuki; wear it only when the Leader permits
   the organisation to be seen. A conical hat with paper veil and bells is issued
   for concealed movement through hostile territory.
2. Ring: a single ring bearing an inscribed character, assigned to a fixed finger.
   The ring is a sealing key for the Gedo Statue. It is organisation property.
   It is never removed, sold, or gambled. Loss of a ring is treated as treason.
3. Forehead protector: your village mark is to be scored through, signifying
   severance. You are a missing-nin now. Your former village is your former life.

Draw nothing on personal loyalty. The organisation is your only affiliation.
